      title: 'Matching, Covering and Packing',
      summary: String.raw`Matchings in bipartite graphs are governed by König's min–max theorem and Hall's marriage condition, both reached by augmenting paths, and stable matchings always exist. In general graphs, Tutte's odd-component condition decides whether a perfect matching exists, refined by the Gallai–Edmonds structure theorem. The chapter then turns to packing and covering: the Erdős–Pósa theorem trades many disjoint cycles against a small set meeting all cycles, the packing-covering theorem of Bowler and Carmesin yields the tree packing and tree covering theorems of Nash-Williams and Tutte at once, and the Gallai–Milgram theorem on path covers implies Dilworth's theorem.`,
